          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 2: Float2 and Float into Float3\n\nIn this example we are constructing a float3 signal by combining a float2 signal and a regular float signal in the Float3 node.\nThe Random node produces a float2 signal which we smooth and connect to the Float3 node.\nThe Sine node produces a float signal which we also connect to the Float3 node.\nThis results in a Float3 signal which we feed to the Phase Offset of the Fractal Noise node."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 683.8809204101562,
          "width": 1514.8109130859375,
          "x": 271.152587890625,
          "y": 1095.2813720703125
